      "topic": "Releases",
      "section": "§6 Specs, tasks and memory",
      "skills": ["dd-release-definition", "dd-release-implement"],
      "justification": "The law states Releases as one bold topic spanning pick, the mandatory grill, SPEC/PLAN/TASKS, implementation, and finalization (memory update -> CLOSURE -> archive) as a single continuous flow, not two separate bold topics. Definition is one lifecycle stage; dd-release-implement (FR10/G12) absorbs both implementation and finalization (memory update, CLOSURE, disposition sweep, artifact GC, archive) as one skill spanning the second stage."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Root cause, always",
      "section": "§7 Quality",
      "skills": ["dd-bug-fix", "dd-diagnose"],
      "justification": "dd-bug-fix (renamed dd-bug-resolution at T-050-21) owns the bug lifecycle -- branch, concurrency, the resolved event and its commit; dd-diagnose owns the diagnosing method itself, phase 0's lineage check through cleanup (FR7/AS-11). One topic, two skills, split by lifecycle vs method."
